lling to further education. Strengths: decision quality, reliability, crew cooperation. Weaknesses: communication, development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Weaknesses: attitude, leadership.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's score roughly:\n\nA: reliability? unorganized, maybe low. Stress? not mentioned. Technical competence: high (anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision). Decision quality? not explicit. Attention? not mentioned. Crew cooperation? leadership good but maybe not. Communication? not mentioned. Responsibility? leadership maybe. Adaptability? not mentioned.\n\nB: reliability high (conscientious). Stress resilience high. Technical competence moderate (weather, computers). Decision quality? not mentioned. Attention? not mentioned. Crew cooperation? uncooperative, grumpy. Communication? not mentioned. Responsibility? not mentioned. Adaptability? not mentioned.\n\nC: reliability 100%. Decision quality high (quick correct). Crew cooperation positive. Communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to learn. Technical competence? not mentioned. Stress? not mentioned. Attention? not mentioned. Responsibility? not mentioned. Adaptability? not mentioned.\n\nD: responsibility high, concentration, problem solving, adaptability (responds to unexpected). Leadership weak, arrogance. Reliability? not mentioned. Stress? responds adequately. Technical competence? problem solving. Decision quality? solves problems extremely well. Crew cooperation? arrogance maybe negative. Communication? not mentioned.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? C has reliability, decision quality, crew cooperation, but communication issues and lack of learning may be problematic for long-distance flights. B has reliability and stress but poor cooperation. D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership. A has technical but organization and feedback issues.\n\nProbably C is strongest overall because reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere are crucial. Communication difficulty could be mitigated, but egocentric and unwillingness to further education are concerns. However, B's uncooperative attitude is also a big issue for crew. D's arrogance also problematic. A's unorganized may affect reliability.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the facts we have so far\". Provide evidence.\n\nLet's produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE stating recommendation for Candidate C, referencing reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, and acknowledging communication concerns.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C."}
